# TalkTally — Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## Executive Summary

TalkTally is a React Native mobile application to help caregivers track and develop early communication skills in toddlers through guided speech detection, automatic recording, and progress tracking. It uses on-device audio metering to detect when a child speaks, records their responses locally, and syncs session summaries to a backend for historical tracking and adaptive recommendations.

## Target Users
- Caregivers (parents, early educators, speech therapists)

## Platforms & Tech Stack
- Mobile: React Native (Expo SDK 54), TypeScript
- Backend: Node.js + Express, PostgreSQL
- State: Zustand
- Audio: Expo Audio

## Core Features
1. Onboarding & Permissions
2. Home with recommended session
3. Calibration & Voice Detection
4. Session flow with prompts, recording, and timeout
5. History & progress tracking
6. Backend session sync

## Session Flow
- Calibration (2s) → Monitoring → Detect speech → Record child audio → Save local file → Log response → Advance step

## Recommendation Engine
- Uses last sessions and accuracy thresholds to suggest next session

## Data Model (summary)
- users: id, device_id, created_at
- sessions: id, device_id, accuracy, total_steps, completed_at

## Privacy & Security (high-level)
- No PII collected or stored on server
- Audio files remain on device
- Device ID used for anonymous tracking

## Acceptance Criteria (MVP)
- Voice detection works on-device
- Sessions recorded and saved locally
- Session summary uploads to backend
- No PII stored or transmitted

